    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE \r\nAT CAHILLY, LISCANNOR, CO. CLARE V95 Y3E6\r\nFOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY. \r\n\r\nON CIRCA 0.754 ACRES  \r\n\r\nCompany license number 003178\r\nVIEWING STRICTLY BY ADVANCED APPOINTMENT WITH SOLE AGENT STREETS AHEAD PROPERTIES\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nStreets Ahead Properties are delighted to bring to the market this detached bungalow on circa 0.754 acres just off the R478 in Liscannor, Co. Clare in a much sought after location on an elevated site.\r\n\r\nLiscannor is a charming coastal village on Ireland’s Wild Atlantic Way, nestled along the dramatic Clare coastline. Surrounded by rugged cliffs, rolling green countryside and the wild beauty of the Atlantic Ocean, it offers a wonderful blend of traditional Irish character and breathtaking scenery.\r\nWith its picturesque harbour, stone buildings and peaceful village atmosphere, Liscannor is a beautiful place to slow down and experience the natural beauty of County Clare. The village is ideally located close to some of Ireland’s most spectacular attractions, including the Cliffs of Moher, Lahinch and the Burren. Whether you’re exploring the coastline, enjoying the fresh sea air, discovering local history or simply taking in the views, Liscannor captures the charm and character of Ireland’s west coast.\r\n\r\nOne of the standout features of this property is its wonderful, elevated outlook across the surrounding countryside and towards the Atlantic Ocean.\r\nFrom the house, the view stretches across a beautiful patchwork of green fields and stone-walled farmland towards the coastline, with the waters of the Atlantic forming a spectacular backdrop. The picturesque landscape changes constantly with the light and weather, from bright blue skies and shimmering waters to the dramatic cloudscapes for which the West Coast is renowned.\r\n\r\nAn early viewing is highly recommended Viewings strictly by advance appointment with sole agent Streets Ahead Properties. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation is comprised of an entrance hallway, sitting room, kitchen/dining, three bedrooms , W.C., and a main bathroom. Teak windows and doors throughout, tiled roof, onsite septic tank and is connected to mains water. There is oil fired central heating and an open fireplace in the sitting room which also heats water and radiators. \r\nExternally there is a landscaped front lawn, ample parking, attached garage, block wall boundary to the front and mature hedging to the front sides and rear. \r\n\r\nBER: E\r\nYEAR OF CONSTRUCTION:  1972\r\nAPPROXIMATE FLOOR AREA: 121.21 SqM\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION – APPROXIMATE DIMENSIONS:\r\n\r\nHallway – T shaped: (5.29m x 1.84m) (1.05m x 1.11m) (7.82m x 1.40m) Laminated timber flooring.\r\n\r\nSitting Room: (4.78m x 3.64m) Dual aspect, front and side. Carpeted flooring. Open fireplace, large windows, hotpress with shelving, door into the dining room.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: (4.11m x 3.29m) Rear aspect, linoleum flooring, eye level and base units, storage press, Door to the rear.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: (3.85m x 3.83m) Front aspect. Laminated timber flooring. Fitted wardrobe and sink.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: (3.69m x 3.26m) Front aspect. Laminated timber flooring. Fitted wardrobe and sink.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: (3.38m x 3.09m) Rear aspect. Laminated timber flooring. Fitted wardrobe.\r\n\r\nW.C.: (3.42m x 1.06m) Tiled flooring and partial wall tiling. Complete with w.c. and w.h.b. Rear aspect.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom: (3.45m x 2.28m) Tiled flooring and partial wall tiling. Storage cupboard shelved for towels. Complete with bath, w.c. and w.h.b.\r\n\r\nAttached garage: (8.49m x 3.21m) Double teak doors to the front, teak doors to the rear. Ample storage, concrete flooring\r\n\r\nShed: (6.27m x 3.02m) Lean to, diesel tank.\r\n\r\n\r\nDisclaimer\r\nNote: Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs are provided for guidance purposes only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious detached family home\r\nWild Atlantic Sea Views of Liscannor Bay and the Lahinch Coastline in the distance.\r\nBright kitchen and dining area\r\nComfortable living room with open fireplace\r\nOil fired central heating\r\nAttached garage.\r\nPivotal location to beaches, villages and towns of North Clare offering incredible convenience to all local amenities.\r\n3 Bedroom property.\r\nCliffs of Moher on your doorstep."
